\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.8}{\ignorespaces Conceptual illustration of an Atomic-Photonic Integrated Circuit. The hybrid device couples a Laser-Written Vapor Cell to external optical components via dedicated interfaces. The working principle is as follows: the NEG dispenser in the reservoir (a) is activated, letting the gas flow through the microchannel (b) to the sensing chambers (c). A specialized waveguide coupler (d) links the sensing region with an external photonic waveguide or fiber assembly (e), creating a functional hybrid atomic chip. Adapted from QSENSATO Srl \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {qsensato_web}.}}{10}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:atomic_pic}{{1.8}{10}{Conceptual illustration of an Atomic-Photonic Integrated Circuit. The hybrid device couples a Laser-Written Vapor Cell to external optical components via dedicated interfaces. The working principle is as follows: the NEG dispenser in the reservoir (a) is activated, letting the gas flow through the microchannel (b) to the sensing chambers (c). A specialized waveguide coupler (d) links the sensing region with an external photonic waveguide or fiber assembly (e), creating a functional hybrid atomic chip. Adapted from QSENSATO Srl \cite {qsensato_web}}{figure.caption.14}{}}
